        "comments": "The assembly drMedTorn1.hap1.1 is based on 35x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Ancient Environmental Genomics Initiative for Sustainability (AEGIS,\nhttps://globe.ku.dk/research/ancient-environmental-genomics-initiative-for-sustainability). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 2 (21.05 Mbp - 27.84 Mbp) are unknown.",
